- Do not use information outside the provided candidates.

Relevance guidance:

- Give the highest scores to candidates whose title or content directly
  describes the problem asked about.
- A candidate that explicitly mentions the queried concept and describes
  the associated problem is more relevant than one that only shares a
  related keyword.
- A candidate that mentions the concept only incidentally should receive
  a lower score.
- Do not prefer a candidate merely because its metadata has a higher
  priority or a more urgent status unless the query asks about priority,
  status, or urgency.
- When several candidates describe the same issue pattern, they may all
  be highly relevant; distinguish them using the actual candidate content,
  not their issue ID.

